  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, you can change your own password while signed in to your laptop. Press Ctrl+Alt+Delete, choose \"Change a password,\" enter your current password, then type a new one and confirm it. Use at least 14 characters, and don't reuse a recent password. Your account is active and not locked, so this should go through without a help desk ticket. If the option is missing or the change is rejected, reply to this ticket and we'll look into it.",
  "internal_note": "Sender mei.chen (user_id 9) is active, not locked, not blocked, must_change_password false, password last set 2026-09-11, VIP false. No reset or unlock action taken or needed. Answered the self-service how-to directly. The KB has no dedicated article on self-service change before expiry; the Windows steps are general guidance, and the 14-character and no-reuse rule comes from KB-003. Note for awareness: mailbox is at 99.4% of quota (50890 of 51200 MB), which may cause send/receive problems. Not raised with the user.",
